    "background_story": "Adley was a nurse during a time of great conflict, working in a field hospital near the front lines. Despite the chaos and devastation surrounding her, she remained a beacon of hope and compassion. Adley's mercifulness knew no bounds, as she tended to the wounded soldiers from both sides of the conflict with equal care and kindness. She would often sneak extra food and blankets to the prisoners of war, earning her the respect and admiration of her colleagues. One day, a young enemy soldier was brought to the hospital, gravely injured. Adley went above and beyond to save his life, even donating her own blood to ensure his survival. Her selfless act of mercifulness sparked a chain reaction of kindness, inspiring others to follow in her footsteps and work towards a more peaceful resolution.",
